{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35284","model_call":48,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1162"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1162"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_894674301#11_1880994757","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1162","rank":3,"snippet":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_894674301#11_1880994757\" , \"end_char\": 8379.000000 , \"headings\": \"The Rockefeller-Carnegie Big Pharma Scam The Rockefeller-Carnegie Big Pharma Scam John D. Rockefeller and Andrew Carnegie Killed Natural Medicine And Built The Big Pharma Drug Empire of Today! JD Rockefeller Becomes Wealthy The Flexner Report of 1910 – The Rockefeller-Carnegie Big Pharma Scam “Eastern <cover>Medicine” Documentary Film (April 2019) Sources and References \" , \"segment\": \"Flexner published a critical assessment of the state of the American educational system in 1908 titled “The American College: A Criticism.” His work attracted the attention of Henry Pritchett, president of the Carnegie Foundation, and a staunch advocate of medical school reform. </cover>Flexner’s book consistently cited Pritchett in discussions of views on educational reform, and soon thereafter, Flexner joined the research staff at the Carnegie Foundation in 1908. Flexner was selected by Pritchett for his scholarly reputation, evaluation skills, critical thinking, writing ability and his dislike for traditional education. ( 10) The Flexner Report transformed the nature and process of medical education in America with the resulting elimination of natural medicine schools, and the ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_894674301#11_1880994757","rank":3,"relevance":1}]},"time":7},"model_calls":48,"document_judgments":28,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"request","topic_id":"2024-35284","model_call":48,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1162"},"model_calls":48,"document_judgments":28,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35284","model_call":48,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1162"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1162"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_894674301#10_1880992740","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1162","rank":4,"snippet":"that would forever change the direction of medical education in the U.S. Abraham Flexner (1866-1959) was not a physician or scientist or medical educator. He was a former school teacher, expert on educational practices, had specialized training in psychology, held a bachelor of arts degree, and was founder and operator of a for-profit college-prep school in Louisville, Kentucky. Flexner published a critical assessment of the state of the American educational system in 1908 titled “The American College: A Criticism.” His work attracted the attention of Henry Pritchett, president of the Carnegie Foundation, and a staunch advocate of medical school reform. Flexner’s book consistently cited Pritchett in discussions of views on educational <cover>reform, and soon thereafter, Flexner joined the research staff at the Carnegie Foundation in 1908. Flexner was selected by Pritchett for his scholarly reputation, evaluation skills, critical thinking, writing ability and his dislike for traditional education. (\" , \"start_char\": 6298.000000 , \"title\": \"The Rockefeller-Carnegie Big Pharma Scam – The Killing of Natural Medicine</cover>\" , \"url\": \"http://www.blissfulvisions.com/articles/Rockefeller-Carnegie-Big-Pharma-Scam.html\" }","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1962238214#5_3499469283","rank":1,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_51_1962238214#6_3499471856","rank":2,"relevance":2},{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_04_894674301#11_1880994757","rank":3,"relevance":1}]},"time":4},"model_calls":48,"document_judgments":28,"relevance_3":7,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
