{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35284","model_call":67,"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"abraham flexner\" \"carnegie foundation\" \"medical education\" \"medical schools\")"},"record":{"query":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"abraham flexner\" \"carnegie foundation\" \"medical education\" \"medical schools\")"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_560026595#15_1170903632","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1178","rank":1,"snippet":": 10000.000000 , \"headings\": \"Medical Education Medical Education MEDICAL EDUCATION The Creation of the Modern Medical School Graduate Medical Education Evolution and Growth The Challenge of Managed Care BIBLIOGRAPHY Medical Education MEDICAL EDUCATION The Social Mandate of Medical Schools Ethical Obligations of Medical Schools Some Ethical Issues Peculiar to Clinical Education Conclusion BIBLIOGRAPHY Medical Education Medical Education MEDICAL TRAINING AT HARVARD Sources Medical Education<cover>MEDICAL EDUCATION bibliography internet resources \" , \"segment\": \"Medical schools, which had existed autonomously during the proprietary era, became closely affiliated with universities and teaching hospitals. No individual contributed more dramatically to the institution-building process than Abraham Flexner (1886– 1959), an educator from Louisville who had joined the staff of the Carnegie Foundation </cover>for the Advancement of Teaching. In 1910, Flexner published a muckraking report, Medical Education in the United States and Canada. In this book, he described the ideal conditions of medical education, as exemplified by the Johns Hopkins Medical School, and the deficient conditions that still existed at most medical schools. Flexner made no intellectual contribution to the discussion of how physicians should be taught, for he adopted the ideas that had ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_39_560026595#15_1170903632","rank":1,"relevance":2}]},"time":140},"model_calls":67,"document_judgments":38,"relevance_3":9,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
