{"actor":"server","event":"response","topic_id":"2024-35284","model_call":87,"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1192"},"record":{"query":{"op":"next","qid":"q1192"},"response":{"burrow":"/data/ssd3/claclark/msm-2.1.burrow","docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_477859414#5_1106006442","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1192","rank":3,"snippet":"GYN How Did Colonial Doctors Work? Pre-Med Colleges in Virginia \" , \"segment\": \"The curriculum expanded to four years. The research arm become prominent and integrated into the medical school's vision. The medical school aligned with a research department was replicated across the country. Standardization: The Flexner Report When Abraham Flexner issued his scathing report in 1910, <cover>Johns Hopkins was the ideal to emulate. Sponsored by the Carnegie Foundation and endorsed by the nascent American Medical Association, the Flexner report examined 155 medical schools, the first survey ever committed. The findings of his exhaustive catalog included lurid descriptions of finding “a room containing a putrid corpse, several of the members of which had been hacked off,” that sent shock waves through the medical profession. His recommendations to reform medical education </cover>with uniform admissions, coursework and graduation requirements, and licensing regulated by the state, were adopted broadly. The demise of the proprietary medical school soon followed. Related Articles Related Medical Schools in the 1930s Related The Impact of Hippocrates in Ancient Greece Related List of Colleges in London, Ontario Related Ultrasound Schools in the Westchester Area Related Dental Universities in the UAE Related The Five ","skipped":[{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_54_477859414#5_1106006442","rank":3,"relevance":3}]},"time":18},"model_calls":87,"document_judgments":48,"relevance_3":15,"max_document_judgments":50,"max_model_calls":100}
